afk: new fix-dispatch template — the fix loop's missing TDD carrier.

Motivation: every other SDD stage has a prompt template that carries its
discipline; the fix stage had only prose, and the prose said "the fixer
fixes, re-runs the tests" — literal fix-then-test. A review finding is a
known, already-observed defect: a test written after the fix passes on
its first run and proves nothing, so a non-fix is indistinguishable from
a fix and the scoped re-review approves it (2026-08-08 incident,
caught by hand before merge). SKILL.md §4 links here
(Template: fixer-prompt.md, via skills-subagent-driven-development.patch)
and re-review-prompt.md verifies the RED evidence this template mandates
(via skills-re-review-prompt.patch).

What must survive a rebase:
- New file under skills/subagent-driven-development/; if upstream ever
  ships its own fix template, reconcile — the per-finding RED -> GREEN
  work order is the point of this file.
- Per-finding cycle, in order: failing test first (extend an existing
  covering test file where one exists), run it and confirm it fails for
  the finding's reason, minimal production fix, re-run green with
  pristine output and neighbours still green.
- `NOT TESTABLE: <why>` escape hatch only for findings with no
  observable behaviour (naming, dead code, comments, pure refactors),
  stated so fixers do not fake evidence.
- Handoff discipline matches the sibling templates: isolated: true as a
  task-tool parameter, agent per SKILL.md Agent Selection (rounds 4-5
  bump one tier), repo-relative [BRIEF_FILE], local:// [REPORT_URI],
  [TEST_FILES] named by the controller, no absolute paths, no git/jj.
- Report contract: a "## Fix Round R" section appended per round with
  per-finding RED (command + failing output + why expected) / GREEN
  (command + passing output) or the NOT TESTABLE line; the short return
  contract matches the implementer template.
- "You Do Not Dispatch Subagents" section, mirroring the contract
  upstream v6.3.0 added to the implementer and reviewer templates: the
  fixer never spawns helpers or a reviewer — the controller's scoped
  re-review is the only review seat for a fix round.

